OpenBonsai adapts the budget manifold operations and projected Gumbel
optimization sequence from src/manifold.py and src/search/quant.py in
openbonsai/allocation.py. Adaptations include tensor-specific integer-byte
costs, ragged candidate sets, conservative budget-feasible decoding, and
a checkpointed assembled-model evaluation context. The discrete decoder
is an independent implementation, not a verbatim copy of upstream's
rounded bit-budget dynamic programs.

Selected quantization primitives under quant/ derive from upstream RCO.
OpenBonsai changes their imports, supported layer geometry, and direct
single-device execution dependencies, and removes import-time changes to
global TF32 flags. openbonsai/candidates.py adds row-chunk execution and
a Cholesky-factor cache around the upstream FastOBQ quantization core.
These changes are not an upstream release, endorsement, or claim of
reproducing reported model quality.
